# Rule 10 note: foreign definitions the 21 sketches read, and their published lemmas

Method: each target's statement and docstring sketch read at the pre-ship tree; for every other-file TCSlib definition
the proof must read, a search for a published lemma named after it (tools/deflemmas.py: theorems whose last name component
starts with <def>_ or <Def>_, in any TCSlib file), cross-checked with check 8 of scripts/campaign_style_lint.py (excerpt below).
This is a reading-based screen. No proofs exist yet, so no sealed compile of the fills was possible; the dl-a corollary's route
probe (route-probe-dla.log) is the one sealed check.

## Missing equation lemmas (prerequisites named in brief.md)
| Definition (file) | Missing | Needed by |
|---|---|---|
| firstHit (Asymptotic/Sampling) | firstHit_eq | dl-a statClose_rejectBlocksL (rejectBlocksL = (firstHit ...).map Fin.val) |
| StatClose (Asymptotic/Sampling) | statClose_iff (introduction; only elimination lemmas exist) | dl-c statClose_sq_generator |
| NUPPT.coinLen (Complexity/Randomized/PPT) | NUPPT.coinLen_eq | dl-a expCollection_sampleClose (coins = n*n); dl-b headline (B's coins); dl-c elGamal_correct, elGamal_secure (coin segments) |
| NUPPT.distinguisherL (Asymptotic/Adversary) | NUPPT.distinguisherL_eq | dl-b headline (A_i inside B); dl-c elGamal_secure |
| predProb, invProb, distAdv (Foundations/Experiments) | predProb_eq, invProb_eq, distAdv_eq | dl-b uprob_trial_ge, uprob_majOracle_ne_le, invProb_shiftInverter_ge; dl-c elGamal_secure (hybrid triangle) |
| Collection.SampleClose, .invProbAt, .HardCore (Asymptotic/Collections) | sampleClose_iff, invProbAt_eq, hardCore_iff (the FunFamily hardCore_iff in Asymptotic/HardCore is a different definition) | dl-a expCollection_sampleClose, expCollection_invProbAt_le; dl-b headline |
| divModStr, xgcdStr, sizeStr, natToList (Candidates/Arithmetic) | divModStr_pairEncode, xgcdStr_pairEncode, sizeStr_eq (only length_sizeStr exists), natToList_eq (= List.ofFn (natToBits k N)) | dl-b polyTimeComputable_halfStr, headline; dl-c polyTimeComputable_egEncRaw, egDecStr_apply, elGamal_correct; sizeStr_eq possibly dl-a/dl-c samplers |
| dlP, dlM, dlG (Candidates/DiscreteLog) | dlP_eq, dlM_eq, dlG_eq (dlP has only dlP_lt_two_pow) | dl-b headline; dl-c polyTimeComputable_egEncRaw, elGamal_correct, elGamal_secure |
| ExpValid, WellFormedIndex, SafePrimeValid, ExpGroupGen.FullLengthExcept, ExpGroupGen.DLHard, ExpGroupGen.dlProb, expF (Candidates/DiscreteLog) | expValid_iff, wellFormedIndex_iff, safePrimeValid_iff, fullLengthExcept_iff, dlHard_iff, dlProb_eq, expF_eq | dl-b headline; dl-c elGamal_correct, elGamal_secure |
| expCollection (Candidates/DiscreteLog, structure-valued) | field equations f, encD, decD, gen, sample (only expCollection_D, expCollection_index exist) | dl-b headline |

For dl-a, Candidates/DiscreteLog and Candidates/Concrete are its own files; it reads Concrete's rejectBlocksL from DiscreteLog through rejectBlocksL_eq (route probe).

## Read through existing lemmas (no prerequisite)
rejectBlocksL (rejectBlocksL_eq, rejectBlocksL_spec), sampleBelowL (sampleBelowL_eq_rejectBlocksL, sampleBelowL_lt), bitsEquiv (bitsEquiv_val),
bitsToNat/listToNat (bitsToNat_eq_listToNat, listToNat_natToList, natToList_length_listToNat), uprob (uprob_bitsToNat_lt, uprob_comp_equiv, ...),
PushesUniform (pushesUniform_of_card_fiber, HardcoreBit.pushesUniform_equiv, ...), QR (mem_QR_iff), sqTo (coe_sqTo), HardcoreBit.majority
(two_mul_card_le_of_majority_ne, uprob_majority_fails_le), leStr/modExpStr/mulStr/addStr/subStr (_pairEncode), decodeFin (decodeFin_ofFn,
ofFn_of_decodeFin_eq_some), padFin (padFin_ofFn, ofFn_padFin_of_le), NUPPT layout (inParam_layout, inArg_layout, inAdvice_layout, inCoins_layout,
runAt_eq, runAtL_ofPolyTime(Uniform), coins_ofPolyTime(Uniform), distinguisher_eq), Ensemble.Indist (Ensemble.indist_iff_exists_negligible),
Negligible (not_negligible_iff), Collection.OneWay (a structure: anonymous constructor), expOrd (expOrd_of_valid/_of_not_valid),
expCollection.D (expCollection_D), Collection.index at expCollection (expCollection_index, expCollection_index_of_lt), dlW (WellFormedIndex.dlW_eq).
uexp has no equation lemma; the sketches use only its lemmas (OneWay.uexp_mono, HardcoreBit.uprob_mul_le_uexp, good_instances).

